{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-koszul-formula","title":"rem:pet-ch2-koszul-formula","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.md","line":321,"body":"","kind":"other","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex#rem:pet-ch2-koszul-formula","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","label":"rem:pet-ch2-koszul-formula","line":664,"source":"\\begin{remark}[Koszul's formula]\n  \\label{rem:pet-ch2-koszul-formula}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0072}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean, def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form, def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor}\n\n  Applying the tensor Lie-derivative formula\n  \\cref{prop:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor-formula} and the exterior-derivative\n  formula \\cref{def:pet-ch2-exterior-derivative-lie-formula} to the Euclidean\n  prototype \\cref{prop:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean} gives\n  \\[\n  \\begin{aligned}\n    (L_Xg)(Y,Z)+(d\\theta_X)(Y,Z)\n      ={}&D_Xg(Y,Z)+D_Yg(X,Z)-D_Zg(X,Y)\\\\\n         &-g([X,Y],Z)-g([Y,Z],X)+g([Z,X],Y).\n  \\end{aligned}\n  \\]\n  This is the Koszul expression determining the Riemannian connection.\n\\end{remark}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Remark</div></section>[Koszul&#x27;s formula] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368322d6b6f737a756c2d666f726d756c61\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0072</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23prop%3Apet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean\">↗ prop:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-dual-one-form\">↗ def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor\">↗ def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor</a> <p></p>Applying the tensor Lie-derivative formula <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23prop%3Apet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor-formula\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor-formula\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368322d6c69652d646572697661746976652d74656e736f722d666f726d756c61\">subsection 1.2</a> and the exterior-derivative formula <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-exterior-derivative-lie-formula\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-exterior-derivative-lie-formula\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368322d6578746572696f722d646572697661746976652d6c69652d666f726d756c61\">subsection 1.2</a> to the Euclidean prototype <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23prop%3Apet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368322d636f76617269616e742d646572697661746976652d696d706c696369742d6575636c696465616e\">subsection 2.1</a> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\begin{aligned}  (L_Xg)(Y,Z)+(d\\theta _X)(Y,Z) ={}&amp; D_Xg(Y,Z)+D_Yg(X,Z)-D_Zg(X,Y)\\\\ &amp; -g([X,Y],Z)-g([Y,Z],X)+g([Z,X],Y). \\end{aligned}  \\]\">\\[  \\begin{aligned}  (L_Xg)(Y,Z)+(d\\theta _X)(Y,Z) ={}&amp; D_Xg(Y,Z)+D_Yg(X,Z)-D_Zg(X,Y)\\\\ &amp; -g([X,Y],Z)-g([Y,Z],X)+g([Z,X],Y). \\end{aligned}  \\]</span> This is the Koszul expression determining the Riemannian connection. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#lem:pet-ch2-extend-tangent-vector","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean","title":"prop:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean","label":"prop:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-implicit-euclidean"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form","title":"def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form","label":"def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor","label":"def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#lem:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection-koszul","title":"lem:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection-koszul","label":"lem:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection-koszul"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#thm:pet-ch2-fundamental-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch2-fundamental-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch2-fundamental-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-christoffel-formula","title":"prop:pet-ch2-christoffel-formula","label":"p